														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842620">
									

<p><a href="/scp-2662">SCP-2662</a> is probably the cleanest execution of the format you're describing, of a humanoid with a disadvantageous anomaly that causes them pain due to its effects on humans. As for your idea, that they're so beautiful that it causes people to commit suicide, I'm not certain that your audience will be able to relate to the character. And that's really what's key here, getting them to experience empathy for the anomaly and his plight.</p>
<p>I'm just not totally convinced that there's much to this story that 2662 (and stories like it) haven't already done.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Objective Beauty is found having been ''kidnapped'' by his obsessed parents until the age of 17.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not&#8230; certain I understand how this is relevant to his condition.</p>
<p>Additionally I should mention that I <em>highly</em> disrecommend using mass suicide as a way to up the stakes for your idea. It's a trope we've seen ten too many times and it seems more dismissive of mental health than anything.</p>

							</div>

								
					
