														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842613">
									

<p>Frankly I think I'd like this more if there weren't some dangerous, hostile nature to the plant. Having the spores communicate to exposed persons what the plant feels, by way of inflicting hunger/thirst/etc. on them is a good enough setup for a narrative as is. You know, there's no need to suddenly introduce a nuclear meltdown to up the stakes and going into the science behind pollination/spore dissemination/neurology is always fun.</p>
<p>I'm a big fan of end-of-article subversions and I think having the plant communicate gratitude to its keepers at a containment site would make for a nice little end-note. Not sure what story it would be preceded by but that's the aspect of the anomaly I'm most interested in — you know, what does a plant feel, what does it have to say, etc., more so than the threat it poses.</p>

