			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842610">
									

<p>1) The user of an SCP doesn't need to be referred to as a -1; that would be for other manifestations or sub-manifestations (such as the figure in the stall).</p>
<p>2) I would make the general equipment limited to just food, medical supplies, and other general emergency equipment. If you tailor the equipment too much to the specific circumstances of the person being saved, then the figure in the stall has no bargaining power; it would be interesting for him to have some at least in order to be able to make deals.</p>
<p>3) I would recommend some sort of countdown; not only does this offer the person in stall more bargaining power, especially if those chasing the person stay around, but also enforces a limit on how long they can stay. It doesn't need to be too short, maybe a couple of hours, but that would up the drama a little.</p>
<p>4) Otherwise, neat idea. There's some interesting story potential, especially if two enemies get locked into it at the same time, which could cause a bidding war as well as any other potential drama. There would also be some interesting potential if the person(s) after the rescued stay around outside.</p>

