<blockquote>
<p>I like the idea of a small story and otherwise basic SCP being the catalyst for one of the Foundation's more compassionate moments in history.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Alright, so bear with me here: I do not think that the Foundation is being particularly kind here. They are at best solving a problem that they created because they knowingly manufactured life by way of the anomaly. These children were not dropped into their laps, as it were, they were the calculated product of a sanctioned laboratory experiment and caring for them isn't particularly nice, it's the bare minimum.</p>
<p>I'd recommend either modifying the anomaly such that the creation of human life can be something unexpected for the Foundation, or shifting focus to whatever uncontained instances of this machine are supposedly walking around, unaware they're robots. You know, the Foundation may care for the children they created but what are they going to do about the septuagenarian cyborgs?</p>

