			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842597">
									

<blockquote>
<p>When you enter the basement of this shack, you enter an endless labyrinth that by all accounts is impossible to escape.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm a tad confused about why you can't just turn around and exit the basement at this point. If there's some spacial anomaly at play, like the exit disappears behind you or something, I worry that will seem rather constructed and unbelieveable.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A lot of this will be exploration logs consisting of different personnel's experiences within the labyrinth, and experiencing how the civilians within live on a day to day basis.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do you intend to make these logs not repetitive? This seems like it's doing something similar to <a href="/scp-3008">SCP-3008</a> in concept, except the monsters have the abilities of changelings, and I'm unconvinced that you'll be able to tell a story with this particularly familiar setup.</p>
<p>Additionally do you have any sort of through-line here? Any central character you want to follow or any specific conflict to overcome?</p>

							</div>

								
					
