														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4842585">
									

<p>The interview was conducted through writing, so the robin physically wrote his responses. It seems obvious to me that if a bird wrote something, it would come out differently than if a human wrote it. This could be due to differences in intelligence, physical ability (I assume the bird was writing with his foot, doesn't sound easy), or just culture. Different dialects exist, and that doesn't make them wrong. Some people spell colour differently, some pronounce keter differently. Yeah, the Foundation COULD retroactively &quot;fix&quot; the bird's different spellings and grammatical choices, but they SHOULDN'T. Because if they did, it would change the reader's perception of the interviewee.</p>
<p>I gave this a solid +1</p>

